1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,277
Why is the sky blue?

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:04,380
On the Moon, it's black.

3
00:00:04,380 --> 00:00:06,028
Even at noon.

4
00:00:06,750 --> 00:00:08,650
The Moon has almost no air.

5
00:00:08,650 --> 00:00:09,683
Earth does.

6
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:13,006
Sunlight looks white,
but it holds every color.

7
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:16,368
Tiny molecules of air
scatter that light.

8
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:19,753
And the shorter the wavelength,
the more it scatters.

9
00:00:20,450 --> 00:00:24,175
Violet light scatters about
ten times more than deep red.

10
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:27,311
So why isn't the sky violet?

11
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:28,980
Sunlight has less violet,

12
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:31,952
and our eyes are
less sensitive to it.

13
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:35,344
So we see blue,
from every direction.

14
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:38,220
At sunset, light crosses more air.

15
00:00:38,220 --> 00:00:40,800
Blue scatters away,
and red gets through.

16
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:43,983
Blue is scattered sunlight.
